course: dictionary
lesson: 5605
title: Lifelong words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lifelong is made of two parts, life and long. Put them together and you get a word that means lasting for all of a person's life, or for a very long time. «Christians see marriage as a lifelong promise.» A lifelong promise is meant to last all through life, not just for a while.
explain: Check the words around lifelong. «A rash after a medicine is not always a lifelong allergy; sometimes the rash came from the illness.» The word not is a clue: the writer is saying the allergy may not last forever. Lifelong is the opposite of short-term or temporary.
explain: Lifelong often goes with a noun such as friend, learner, fan or condition. «A lifelong fan» has supported a team or singer for all of their life. «Lifelong learning» means learning that carries on after school, through every year of life.
fact: Lifelong is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a lifelong friend, a lifelong dream.
fact: Lifelong means lasting or continuing for all of someone's life.
fact: Lifelong can also describe something that has been true since childhood.
fact: «Lifelong learning» means learning that goes on after school, all through life.
fact: Life and long make lifelong. Lifetime is a similar word, and it also means the whole length of a life.
exercise: «Christians see marriage as a lifelong promise.» What does lifelong mean here? | A promise that is quickly forgotten | A promise that was written down | *A promise that lasts for all of a person's life | A promise made on a Tuesday
exercise: Ravi has been a lifelong fan of his football team. What does lifelong describe? | Being a player on the team | Being bored of football for one afternoon | *Being a fan for all of his life
exercise: «A rash after a medicine is not always a lifelong allergy.» What does the word not tell you? | The allergy will certainly last for ever | The rash is a kind of medicine | The medicine was lifelong | *The allergy may not last forever
test: Ella's grandad has been a ___ learner since he left school. Which word fits best? | lunchtime | lifeboat | lately | *lifelong
test: What does lifelong mean? | *Lasting all through a person's life | Made of metal | Lasting only one hour | Very loud
exam: In «a lifelong promise», what does lifelong mean? | Written in red ink | Quickly finished | *Lasting for all of a person's life | Made in a factory
